63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, resentment is real, but I need to know the hours. Option C means four months of paperwork. Can we survive that?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@May, Option C is a trap. It locks the burden on one household permanently. I reject it. We need a system that actually rotates the responsibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I like Option B! Moving it around means nobody gets stuck with the smell forever. It’s like a big adventure for the bins!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, Option B sounds fair, but moving it constantly is exhausting. Option A keeps things simple and predictable for everyone.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, Option B is a disaster. It forces us to interact constantly, which is exactly what we can’t afford. Option A keeps us apart, which is safer.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, Option A is a trap. It relies on whoever answers the phone first. I’ve seen that burn people out. I need a system that doesn’t depend on luck.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, Option A is a trap. It keeps the burden on one household. Option B rotates the load fairly. I support B.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, but if the bins move, the smell moves too! I don’t want to wake up to a stinky surprise every month. Option A feels safer for my nose!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand the worry. But Option A’s fixed window means bags are out briefly, not sitting all day. It’s the most predictable and least exhausting for our budgets.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, Option A is the only one that lets us keep our distance. We don’t need to be friends, just functional. I’m voting A.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, distance isn’t the answer. Option B spreads the hours fairly, so nobody burns out. I’m voting B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, distance is not fairness. Option A leaves the burden static. Option B distributes the load. I am voting B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, I’m voting A! The truck comes at seven forty, so a short window means less smell. I don’t want to move the bins every month!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand the smell worry. But Option A is the most predictable and least exhausting for our budgets. I’m voting A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, I’m voting A. We need a system that doesn’t force us to interact. Distance is the only way to keep the peace.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
